#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kmyapplication; Handbook"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kmyapplication; is the server component of the Simon speech recognition "
"suite. It handles the recognition and the model compilation and receives it "
"input from the Simon client(s) which connect to the server using TCP/IP."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information please see the <ulink url=\"help:/simon/overview."
"html#architecture\">Simon manual</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &kmyapplication;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Simond is a command line application which does not have any user interface. "
"There are no special launch parameters."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"However, Simond installs a KCM that is listed in KDEs systemsettings and can "
"also be accessed directly using the <command>kcmshell4</command>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid "kcmshell4 simondconfiguration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Because Simond compiles the speech model (if instructed to do so by the "
"Simon client(s)), the configuration of the speech model compilation is of "
"course also relevant when administrating Simond. You can open it by using "
"<command>kcmshell4</command>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "kcmshell4 simonmodelcompilationconfig"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When used from within a graphical environment (if you don't know what this "
"is you are most likely using one), it is recommended to use the graphical "
"frontend called <command>ksimond</command> which also provides access to the "
"configuration modules through its configuration dialog. See the KSimond "
"manual for details."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid "User Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using the user configuration you can define, edit and remove users and their "
"models from the server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screenshot of the Simond user configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid "Simond user configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Simond identifies its connections with a user / password combination which "
"is completely independent from the underlying operating system and its users "
"(which means you have to have at least one Simond user set up to use it). "
"Every Simon client logs onto the server with a user / password combination "
"which identifies a unique user and thus a unique speech model."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The users are stored in a sqlite database that is managed through the "
"<command>simonduserconfiguration</command> KCM."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid "This database is stored depending on your operating system:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid "Simond user database storage"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:125 index.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid "Microsoft Windows"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:126 index.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid "GNU/Linux"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: index.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid "%appdata%\\.kde\\share\\apps\\simond\\simond.db"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: index.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid "~/.kde/share/apps/simond/simond.db"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Simond does come with a default user so you don't have to add a user before "
"you can connect Simon to the Simond server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The default user name is \"default\" and the password is \"nopassword\"."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The password of the users will be hashed and cannot be shown in cleartext. "
"When a user forgets his or her password there is no way to retrieve the "
"original password from the Simond database but you can reset it using the "
"\"Change Password\" button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When removing a user from the database which already has a speech model "
"associated with him, you will be prompted if you also want to remove the "
"model. If you select no and add a user with the same name later on, he will "
"start off with this speech model."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:147
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When selecting the <guibutton>Keep recognition samples</guibutton> option "
"the samples the recognition works on are not deleted. This means that during "
"normal operation, users will gather everything they say with the most likely "
"transcription returned by &kmyapplication;. This can be used to "
"automatically gather training data while using Simon. The samples will be "
"stored in different locations depending on your operation system:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid "Simond recognition sample storage"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: index.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"%appdata%\\.kde\\share\\apps\\simond\\models\\(user)\\recognitionsamples"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: index.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid "~/.kde/share/apps/simond/models/(user)/recognitionsamples"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When multiple clients connect to Simond with the same username "
"simultaneously, they will use a joint recognition instance. In practice, "
"this means that multiple clients can provide audio data (multiple "
"microphones) and all connected clients with the same username will receive "
"all results of this data. To avoid this behavior and instead force separate "
"recognition paths, activate <guibutton>Isolated Mode</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid "Network Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using the network configuration, the user can change the port used by the "
"server and restrict access to a specific IP."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you don't know what hosts, ports or IPs are it is very likely that the "
"default values are just fine."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:179
#, no-c-format
msgid "screenshot of the Simond network configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid "Simond network configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The port can be changed freely. The default of 4444 is however not occupied "
"by any major application or protocol and thus recommended. If you adjust the "
"port here, make sure you also make the necessary adjustments on your Simon "
"clients."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using the option to \"Only allow connections from\" you can restrict the "
"access to your server from anywhere but the given IP address. By default "
"this is configured to only allow (Simon) connections from the local host "
"which only allows for local Simon clients to connect to the server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is simply a security measure because it effectively blocks connections "
"from anywhere else (even if the attacker knows your Simon username and "
"password). To allow connections from other hosts simply uncheck the checkbox."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Furthermore, write access can be restricted to a specific host. This allows "
"to run \"public\" servers, where users can connect and use the recognition "
"but are not allowed to initiate any form of synchronization."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:198
#, no-c-format
msgid "Protocol encryption is not yet implemented."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid "Speech Model Compilation Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid "Simon compiles the speech model by utilizing external software."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"While Simon will find the needed executables automatically if they are in "
"your systems path, you can also override those automatic values in this "
"configuration page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can also change the selected recognition backend in case of user "
"generated models. Depending on your Simon installation, not all backends "
"might be available."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screenshot of the speech model compilation configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid "Simond speech model configuration"
msgstr ""

